# What a deploy must not upload. Both `agents-cli deploy` and `gcloud` read this
# file in preference to .gitignore once it exists, so it includes .gitignore
# rather than restating it: a project keeps one list of build output and one
# list of things that are merely not worth uploading.
#!include:.gitignore

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# Extensions are vendored into the repository and committed, but the deployed
# agent never reads them: `agents-cli install` restores them from the pins in
# agents-cli-extensions.yaml, and their code runs on the developer's machine.
# Uploading them costs image size and ships their sources with the agent.
/extensions/

# Files `scaffold enhance` moved aside from a repo it adopted, which can include
# the old .env.
/.agents-cli-original/
